WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.470
- Anytime you watch a Halloween movie,

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:02.490
you know there are going to be Easter eggs

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:03.660
in honor of John Carpenter,

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.040
the director of the original "Halloween,"

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.870
and creator of that iconic soundtrack.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.120
Scoring movies was not
Carpenter's only musical endeavor.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:09.953
He also had a band,

00:00:09.953 --> 00:00:12.750
which we see covered in the
pub scene in Halloween Kills.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:18.830
♪ Daddy don't take it hard when you cry ♪

00:00:21.011 --> 00:00:24.870
♪ Mama tears you apart, when she lies ♪

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.490
They're singing "She
Don't Want You Anymore"

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.013
by The Coupe De Villes.

00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:33.013
♪ Daddy don't take it hard when you cry. ♪

00:00:34.684 --> 00:00:39.684
♪ Mama tears you apart, when she lies. ♪

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.820
This band consists of
Carpenter, Nick Castle,

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.140
who played Michael Myers in the original

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.300
and parts of the new trilogy,
and Tommy Lee Wallace,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.620
the production designer of the original

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.030
and director of "Halloween III."

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.560
These mermaid triplets were not the only

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.840
John Carpenter reference
in this talent show.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.809
♪ I think I'll break
up with my girlfriend ♪

00:00:55.809 --> 00:01:00.199
♪ Her antics are queer, I'll admit ♪

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:03.972
♪ Each time I say darling I love you ♪

00:01:03.972 --> 00:01:07.170
♪ She tells me that I'm full of sh-- ♪

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.460
The song is called "Shaving Cream,"

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.170
and it was originally
aired by a radio host

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.940
known as Dr. Demento before being released

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.940
on a compilation album called
Dr. Demento's Dementia Royale.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.470
In "Halloween" and "Halloween II,"

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.490
there's a special on TV

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.740
called Dr. Dementia's
horror movie marathon.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:23.040
- I plan on making popcorn
and watching Doctor Dementia.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.320
Six straight hours of horror movies.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.600
Little Lindsey Wallace
won't know what hit her.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.860
To learn how "Halloween Kills"

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.320
answered a question that never
fully made sense in the original,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.300
how Karen shares a connection
with her counterpart

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.490
from another timeline, Easter
eggs from the deleted scenes

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.680
and all of the Halloween
franchise references,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.188
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:40.188 --> 00:01:42.938
(dramatic music)

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.130
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.089
Evil dies tonight.

00:01:50.089 --> 00:01:51.576
- [Marion] Evil dies tonight.

00:01:51.576 --> 00:01:53.392
- [Tommy] Evil dies tonight!

00:01:53.392 --> 00:01:55.077
- [Woman] Evil dies tonight!

00:01:55.077 --> 00:01:56.564
- [Brackett] Evil dies tonight!

00:01:56.564 --> 00:01:58.015
- [Tommy] Evil dies tonight!

00:01:58.015 --> 00:01:59.820
- [Crowd] Evil dies tonight!

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.597
- Spoiler alert, he didn't die.

00:02:01.597 --> 00:02:04.530
"Halloween Kills: is the direct
sequel to "Halloween" 2018.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.240
David Gordon Green would return to direct

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.230
and co-write the screenplay

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.030
with Danny McBride and Scott Teems.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.050
As the title would imply,

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.790
this entry would focus more on the kills,

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.190
but also on returning
characters from the original,

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.423
most of whom get killed.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.184
Later in this episode, I'll
be joined by Jimmy Champane

00:02:18.184 --> 00:02:20.087
who will talk about the
little details that secretly

00:02:20.087 --> 00:02:22.710
set up aspects of the
finale, "Halloween Ends."

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.912
Let's get into the Things You Missed.

00:02:24.912 --> 00:02:27.329
(soft music)

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.790
The opening shot shows us some balloons.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.260
I couldn't help but notice that the colors

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.270
are the same colors as
the Letterboxd logo.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:37.590
Letterboxd is a social media site

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.180
where you can log all
the movies you watch,

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.010
so it's almost as if
this is a subtle reminder

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.930
to log "Halloween Kills" on Letterboxd.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.640
I don't know if this was
actually the intention,

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.500
but if it was, it's a
clever way to remind people

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.050
to give this movie some free
advertising on social media.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.360
They just might want to do
it at the end next time,

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.260
not the beginning.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.480
This shot leads to Cameron
discovering Deputy Hawkins

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.470
where we last left him,

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.360
injured on the street
in the previous movie.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.950
I'm surprised Cameron
didn't brush this off

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.410
as a Halloween prank of some
kind, but lucky for Hawkins,

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.760
Cameron is able to get him help.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.040
We flash back to Halloween night in 1978,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.720
where a group of cops meet up in an alley

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.540
and Hawkins says he saw Michael
cross through and disappear.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.130
Chronologically, this scene takes place

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.720
right after the original "Halloween."

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.670
On another timeline, in "Halloween II,"

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.800
we see an alternate version
of the events where Michael,

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.780
similarly, cuts through
an alley to escape.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.220
As I mentioned in my last video,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.770
Lonnie Elam is a character from
the original, he's this kid,

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.660
but here we can also see
the Smith's Grove car

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.950
that Michael stole in "Halloween"

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.420
now parked outside of the Myers house,

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.228
which means at some point
after getting shot by Loomis,

00:03:29.228 --> 00:03:31.170
he drove the car back to his home.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.150
There is another clue
that Michael returned home

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.620
that can be seen when Hawkins and McCabe

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.260
go to investigate the house
and enter Judith's old room.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.880
The right window is now closed.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.160
In "Halloween," we saw Sam
Loomis and Sheriff Brackett

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.840
visit the room earlier that same night,

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.640
and in that scene, the window was open.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.290
Everything else about this set in Kills

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.180
was carefully matched to
the set from "Halloween,"

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.520
from the wallpaper to the
broken window on the left

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.590
to the exact lamp on Judith's desk,

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.390
so this closed window must be a suggestion

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.370
that Michael came home and closed it.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.140
Anyone who noticed this
may start to wonder

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.730
where the Boogeyman is hiding.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.350
That question would be answered

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.760
when he pops out to attack McCabe,

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.100
one of the few instances where
we see Michael Myers run.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.750
And if you look closely,
you'll notice he attempts

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.820
to strangle the officer
with a length of rope.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.710
This answers a question
that fans have always had

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.150
since the original "Halloween."

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.680
When Michael broke into
the hardware store,

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.902
Sheriff Brackett describes
the items that were stolen.

00:04:15.902 --> 00:04:17.803
- All they took was some Halloween masks,

00:04:17.803 --> 00:04:20.160
a rope and a couple of knives.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.570
- [Narrator] We see Michael wear the mask.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.370
We see him use the knives, but until now,

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.020
we never saw the rope,
though you could say

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.270
that it was used to tie Bob
upside down in the closet.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:28.950
That's what I think the
purpose of the rope was,

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.590
but it's cool to see a second
use for it here in Kills.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.600
It was also very clever
writing to have Hawkins

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.490
be the one to kill his
partner rather than Michael,

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.412
because it means that this
line from "Halloween" 2018

00:04:37.412 --> 00:04:39.540
is technically still true.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:42.540
- [Laurie] Michael Myers
murdered five people.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.830
- If Michael had killed McCabe,

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:44.940
that would have been six.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.410
It would have screwed everything up.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.540
You can sit back down now, CinemaSins.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:49.560
The flashback scene ends

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.124
just as the opening scene
from the original movie did,

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.800
with Michael walking outside

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.870
and standing in front of his
house with a blank expression,

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:55.830
where the camera pulls back

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.870
and he's eventually captured by police.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.640
That takes us to the
opening title sequence,

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.290
which features several
burning jack-o'-lanterns

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.030
to represent the fire
that Michael was left in

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.170
at the end of the last movie.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.510
There are 12 in all, each
progressively more burnt,

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.650
perhaps because "Halloween Kills"

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:09.300
is number 12 in the franchise.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.980
If they really wanted to get metaphorical,

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:11.940
they could have made number eight

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.193
a pile of poop instead
of a jack-o'-lantern.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.370
The bar where several of our
returning characters convene

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.080
is an Irish Pub known as Mick's

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.790
with a horseshoe and shamrock on the sign.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.267
This is probably a small
nod to the original

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:23.940
"Halloween" timeline,
which used Celtic lore

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.290
to explain Michael's condition.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.030
In "Halloween II," the
source of Michael's power

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.860
is the Gaelic festival of Samhain.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:29.730
- [Loomis] Sam hain.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.320
- [Zac] In "Halloween
III," it is the motivation

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.433
for Conal Cochrane's evil plans.

00:05:32.433 --> 00:05:33.900
And in "Curse of Michael Myers,"

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.843
the dates of Michael's attacks
are tied to constellations

00:05:35.843 --> 00:05:38.070
and ancient festivals of Celtic legend.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.466
I go in depth on this lore in each of my

00:05:39.466 --> 00:05:41.340
Things You Missed
episodes on those movies,

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.840
but for the purposes of "Halloween Kills,"

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.120
all you have to know is that
Samhain eventually transformed

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.370
into the holiday that
we know as Halloween,

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.110
the title of this franchise.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:50.745
As I mentioned in the
last episode, this couple,

00:05:50.745 --> 00:05:52.290
dressed as a nurse and doctor,

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.120
briefly appeared in "Halloween" (2018),

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.100
likely as a reference to
the original "Halloween II,"

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.562
which featured Michael
taking out Dr. Mixter

00:05:57.562 --> 00:05:59.820
and his staff of sl*t nurses.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.290
Their names are Vanessa and Marcus.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.150
And Marcus, like in "Halloween" 2018,

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.976
can never seem to
remember his stethoscope.

00:06:04.976 --> 00:06:06.110
- [Marcus] Wait, hang on, hang on.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.866
I don't have my stethoscope.

00:06:07.866 --> 00:06:09.660
Sh*t, I forgot my stethoscope.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.550
- Just as they were teased
in the previous film

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.110
before becoming actual characters,

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.340
they tease a character coming up

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.260
in the next movie "Halloween Ends."

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:17.370
- Yeah, no, that's right.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.690
You're right, stand up for myself.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.157
Tomorrow morning I'm gonna go in there...

00:06:20.157 --> 00:06:22.500
- You will punch Dr. Mathis in the face.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.109
- [Zac] Apparently Dr.
Mathis has been casted

00:06:24.109 --> 00:06:26.320
and will be a character
in the final installment.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.710
But there's also a more significant detail

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:30.360
about Marcus and Vanessa that you probably

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.572
didn't think about the first time though.

00:06:32.572 --> 00:06:35.155
(tense music)

00:06:37.666 --> 00:06:41.550
(suspenseful music)

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.770
In my Things You Missed
episode on "Halloween" 2018,

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.780
I talked about how Laurie Strode
tried to reverse the roles

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.190
between herself and Michael Myers

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.080
to make her the hunter and him the hunted.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:50.040
To symbolize this switch,

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:51.780
there are many other role
reversals in the movie,

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.490
like Allyson and Cameron's
Halloween costumes

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:55.260
being a gender swapped Bonnie and Clyde.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.963
We see the trend continue
here in "Halloween Kills"

00:06:56.963 --> 00:06:58.410
with Marcus and Vanessa.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.720
Marcus is dressed as a doctor
and Vanessa as a nurse,

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.850
which are the opposite
of their actual jobs.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:03.683
- I'm a doctor.

00:07:03.683 --> 00:07:05.340
My husband's a nurse.
- I should've guessed.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:06.270
- Another pair of characters

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:07.710
are swapped in a similar fashion.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:09.480
Big John and Little John
are the current residents

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:10.410
of the Myers House.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.330
At one point, we see them
standing side by side,

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.460
and Little John is a lot
taller than Big John.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:15.960
Unless the names are talking about their-

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.730
When the two are eventually
killed by Michael Myers,

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:19.650
they die in the same positions
as the framed photograph

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.080
in the upstairs office, but
their places are swapped.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.820
Because "Halloween Kills"
and "Halloween Ends"

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.800
both began pre-production
shortly after "Halloween" 2018,

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.530
there is a lot more continuity
among the three films

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.390
than we've seen before in this franchise.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:31.830
Being an authority on this franchise,

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.840
my friend Jimmy Champane
is the perfect person

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.400
to tell you about some of those details

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.650
and why some of them are gonna
be important going forward.

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:38.910
- Something that makes this movie feel

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.590
like more than the sum of its parts to me

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:43.140
outside of the attention to
detail during the flashback

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.670
is how much continuity there is

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.550
between "Halloween" 2018
and "Halloween Kills."

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:48.383
There are also other setups

00:07:48.383 --> 00:07:50.347
that are supposed to
be significant in Ends.

00:07:50.347 --> 00:07:53.850
In Mick's Bar, we see a poster
for the local radio station,

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:57.990
94.9 WURG the Urge with Willie the kid.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.820
Later on, when Mr. Tovoli breaks into

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.080
Marcus and Vanessa's car,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:04.267
we hear the radio DJ say
the same channel name.

00:08:04.267 --> 00:08:06.989
- [Announcer] WURG 94.9,

00:08:06.989 --> 00:08:11.040
giving you the urge with Willie the Kid.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.870
- This could tie into the big radio tower

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.090
we see at various points
throughout Haddonfield

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:18.150
in "Halloween Kills,"
even the 1978 flashback,

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:20.610
which seems to be hinted
at possibly being a part

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.831
of "Halloween Ends" in
the commentary track.

00:08:22.831 --> 00:08:24.990
- [Jamie Lee Curtis] What are
you up with this radio tower?

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:28.198
Is it it gonna be in the 3rd movie
Dave? - [Judy Greer] Now it's the
only thing I'm going to notice.

00:08:28.198 --> 00:08:29.031
- [Green] I don't know...

00:08:29.031 --> 00:08:29.970
- [Jimmy] And speaking of Mr. Tivoli,

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.850
we see him during the intro
scene of "Halloween" 2018

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.850
before Aaron and Dana meet
Michael Myers for the first time.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.860
Before the encounter,
Doctor Sartain mentions

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:39.060
that they should tie their shoes

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.160
because he has a fixation with laces.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.140
And then when we see him
in "Halloween Kills,"

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:44.880
there's a quick insert shot where we see

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.141
that he is wearing Vans slip-ons.

00:08:46.141 --> 00:08:48.930
And then finally, his
umbrella is found in the car.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.910
Sticking with Kills,
Big John and Little John

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.680
have a sign tucked away in their office

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.390
for Big John and Little John realty.

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:56.580
We also see that same sign when Tommy

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.160
is rounding up locals to
hunt down Michael Myers.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:00.930
And then of course,
there's also a similar ad

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.550
on the corkboard by their front door.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:04.710
This backstory for the
characters works super well

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.300
because it explains why they would ever

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.830
want to live in the Myers' house.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:10.230
They probably got it for a
steal because it was vacant

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.790
for so long, but I'm just glad
we didn't get a cliche line

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.670
about that in the movie like we would

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:16.620
in pretty much any other horror movie,

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.870
and it's all given to
us through context clues

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.000
with props inside their actual house

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.350
and throughout the rest of the movie.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.120
I also personally like it a lot more

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.830
than what we got in the original timeline

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.200
with John Strode moving
into the Myers house,

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.930
"The Myers house", where
he also seems to be running

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.400
his own realty business.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.530
Or at the very least, he
probably got a good deal

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:37.290
on the joint from his brother
who is definitely a realtor.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.970
- So in a way, Big John and Little John

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.130
are the spiritual
successors to John Strode?

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.470
- Yeah, they even share the
similarity of being victims

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.900
of Halloween pranks played
by trick-or-treaters.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.850
- Now, you stinking kids
got about three seconds

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.256
to get the hell off my property.

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:51.964
One, two-

00:09:51.964 --> 00:09:53.836
- Get out of my yard, you little perverts!

00:09:53.836 --> 00:09:55.813
(group screaming)

00:09:55.813 --> 00:09:57.720
- I never understood why
he calls them perverts.

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:59.070
All they did was steal candy.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.990
But I do kind of understand
why they made a reference

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.460
to a character from "Halloween 6:

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.600
The Curse of Michael Myers."

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:05.940
It's because "Halloween Kills"
shares a huge similarity

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.620
with that movie in that
these are the only two

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.290
Halloween films where Tommy
Doyle comes back as an adult.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:12.030
They actually considered
bringing back Paul Rudd

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.070
to play him again, but it
seems like it didn't work out,

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.540
probably for the same
reason they didn't want

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:18.030
Laurie's daughter to be named
Jamie in "Halloween" 2018.

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:19.830
It would just be confusing for casual fans

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:22.020
to have strong elements of
another timeline like that.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:23.580
So instead, they loaded up the movie

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.190
with more covert
"Halloween 6" Easter eggs.

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.760
- [Laurie] People are afraid.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.360
That is the true curse of Michael.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.400
- Or, you know, not so covert.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.440
Another similarity between
the two adult Tommys

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.273
is their weapons.

00:10:35.273 --> 00:10:37.410
In Kills, Tommy sticks with
his trusty baseball bat,

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:38.970
despite having access to guns.

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:40.380
This reminds me of the end of Curse

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:41.400
where in the theatrical cut,

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.170
Tommy beats down Michael
Myers with a pipe,

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:45.120
which he swings around
like a baseball bat.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.190
I also think the scene where
Tommy breaks Old Huckleberry

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:48.660
off its moorings is symbolic.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.760
All these legacy characters
have waited years and years

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:52.770
in Haddonfield, and now
they'll finally get to jump

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:54.300
into action to fight Michael Myers.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.910
However, many of them would
suffer a similar fate.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.560
This would be the fourth
time Nancy Stephens

00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:59.970
was cast to play Marion Chambers.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.430
She was in "H20," "Halloween
II" and, of course,

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.080
the original, where she
was attacked by Michael

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:04.913
from the car.

00:11:04.913 --> 00:11:07.170
He climbs on top the vehicle
and reaches down to grab her.

00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:08.410
This time, he uses the same tactic

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:10.500
by mounting the SUV she's traveling in,

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.060
punching through that
passenger side window

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.560
and reaching in to get his hands on her,

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.570
but this time Nurse
Chambers doesn't make it.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:17.070
Michael stabs Marcus in the eye,

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.200
like what he did to Dr.
Mixter in "Halloween 2,"

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:21.660
then kicks open the car door
on Vanessa for his finest,

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.150
and also maybe funniest kill of all time.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.950
Lindsey Wallace has her
own encounter with Michael

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.600
shortly after where she's being choked,

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:30.090
but manages to get away
by peeling his mask off.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:31.650
She probably picked this up from Laurie,

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:34.260
who did just that to escape
Michael's grasp in the original.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.660
One of the kills earlier in
the movie is also a callback.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:39.420
We meet the ex-firefighter Phil
Larson and his wife, Sondra,

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.880
who, by the way, was the
gravekeeper from "Halloween" 2018.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.160
Michael kills Phil by reaching
through the door to grab him.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:46.590
We've seen him do this a
number of times, most notably,

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:47.970
through the closet in "Halloween"

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.370
and through Laurie's front
door in "Halloween" 2018.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:53.100
While this next one isn't a
kill and isn't Michael Myers,

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.110
there is a callback when
Vanessa leaves the bar

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.340
and rushes to her car.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:57.930
We see the windows are all fogged up,

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:59.760
signaling that someone is hiding inside,

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.080
just like when Michael stakes out

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:03.810
inside of Annie's car in "Halloween" 1978.

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:05.610
At the end, Allyson falls down the stairs,

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:06.960
just like Laurie did in the original.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:08.580
Karen stabs Michael with a pitchfork,

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.040
just like Michael did to
Spitz in "Halloween 5."

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.140
And this guy brings a hockey
stick to fight Michael,

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.150
just like the kid at the beginning of H20.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:17.880
I guess that's still more
reasonable than this lady,

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.710
who brings an iron to fight Michael Myers,

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.906
a character so great that
fans started calling her

00:12:21.906 --> 00:12:24.150
The Iron Maiden of Haddonfield.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.100
- Hi guys, this is Belissa Lea

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:29.700
and I am the Iron Maiden of Haddonfield.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.111
- New "Halloween Ends"
poster just dropped.

00:12:31.111 --> 00:12:33.360
In actuality though,
people are going to riot

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:34.220
if she's not in the movie.

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:36.090
At the very least, they
could throw her a cameo

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:37.470
in the news or something in the same way

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:39.330
that Julian got a little
screen time in Kills

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.280
after being a popular
character in the last film.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.620
Best case scenario though,
the Iron Maiden rises

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:45.930
from the dead to kill
Michael Myers with her iron.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:47.490
The mob that the Iron Maiden is seen in

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.290
is a continuation of the mob from the bar.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:52.584
And if we look closely, we can
discover even more secrets.

00:12:52.584 --> 00:12:55.167
(tense music)

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:03.300
You know, as far as extras go,

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.340
The Iron Maiden of Haddonfield
gets all the support,

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.350
but I personally think
the guy who realized

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:08.940
moving to Haddonfield was a huge mistake

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:10.170
deserves some love as well.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:12.360
He's part of the mob of
vigilantes who come out of the bar

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.100
and into town seeking retribution.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.110
In case there was any doubt
that this is, in part,

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.100
the same group from the bar,

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.170
we've got this lady repping
the Mick's Bar merch.

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:20.250
Buy dat merch.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.690
This group's existence is a reference

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.460
to "Halloween 4: Return of Michael Myers,"

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.230
where we see a good ol'
group of Illinois boys

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:26.940
storm out of the bar to hunt down Michael,

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:29.563
but they accidentally kill
Ted Hollister instead.

00:13:29.563 --> 00:13:31.671
(sad piano music)

00:13:31.671 --> 00:13:33.210
What happens here is pretty similar.

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.880
In Kills, they go after Mr.
Tivoli, who jumps out the window

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.659
to avoid being massacred by the mob.

00:13:37.659 --> 00:13:38.692
(sad piano music)

00:13:38.692 --> 00:13:39.930
- God damn.

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:41.010
- These new Illinois boys

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:43.530
actually spend most of the
movie chasing the wrong guy.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.360
Between that, the fact
that Officer Hawkins

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.460
accidentally shoots his own
partner while aiming for Michael

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:49.080
and this line from Brackett...

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:51.750
- [Brackett] Now he's
turning us into monsters.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.360
- The idea of hysteria and
outrage being just as dangerous

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:57.030
as a serial killer is more
prevalent here than ever before.

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:58.470
This is fitting for a Halloween movie

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:00.540
released in the era of cancel culture.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:03.270
People even tried to cancel
this movie multiple times.

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:04.830
Yeah, these cancel culture people

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:06.540
are (beep) deranged losers.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:08.310
Whether it's an intentional
message by the writers

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:10.687
or just a natural product of
trying to portray our society,

00:14:10.687 --> 00:14:12.510
I find it fitting that "Halloween Kills"

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:14.910
highlights a societal issue
relevant to the time period,

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.800
following in the footsteps
of the original "Halloween,"

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:19.230
which I talked about in my
Halloween Things You Missed.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:20.635
One thing that can be
confusing for some people

00:14:20.635 --> 00:14:22.946
is the Halloween timeline,
or as I sometimes call it,

00:14:22.946 --> 00:14:25.470
The Halloween Express, all aboard.

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:27.187
The current timeline includes "Halloween,"

00:14:27.187 --> 00:14:30.450
"Halloween" 2018, "Halloween
Kills" and "Halloween Ends."

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:32.029
It does not include
"Halloween II," however.

00:14:32.029 --> 00:14:34.200
In the pub scene where
Tommy introduces Lindsey

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:35.940
to the crowd, he mentions
how her babysitter,

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:36.900
Annie, was killed.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:39.027
The movie shows us a couple
shots of Annie from "Halloween,"

00:14:39.027 --> 00:14:41.139
and then curiously, this shot of her

00:14:41.139 --> 00:14:43.140
on the stretcher in "Halloween II."

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.390
While "Halloween II" is still
not a part of this timeline,

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:46.890
it makes sense that this part of the story

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:49.530
would have happened anyway
on route to "Halloween" 2018.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.510
On a similar note, much
of this movie takes place

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.817
at Haddonfield Memorial Hospital,
which shares the same name

00:14:53.817 --> 00:14:56.100
and logo as the hospital
in "Halloween II."

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.420
But again, I think we can just assume

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.720
this hospital already existed,

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:00.840
even if it wasn't shown
in the first movie.

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.547
I know this caused a little
bit of confusion for some,

00:15:02.547 --> 00:15:04.110
but look at it like this.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:04.943
In the original,

00:15:04.943 --> 00:15:06.930
Laurie had a crush on
this boy named Ben Tramer.

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:08.321
- [Laurie] I'd rather
go out with Ben Tramer.

00:15:08.321 --> 00:15:09.600
- [Zac] But in "Halloween II,"

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.014
which takes place the same
night, Tramer is killed.

00:15:12.014 --> 00:15:14.490
(explosion roaring)

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:17.250
So Tramer died at about 17
years old in that timeline.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.472
However, in Kills, Hawkins
tells the story of one night

00:15:19.472 --> 00:15:21.240
when he was out with Laurie at a bar,

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:23.520
but didn't get past first base because...

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:28.142
- I knew you were sweet for Ben Tramer.

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:31.290
- In the US, you have to
be at least 21 years old

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:33.060
to go to a bar, so this
implies that Tramer

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:36.030
at least lived to see 21
and may still be alive,

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:38.439
which I'm sure Jimmy
is very excited about.

00:15:38.439 --> 00:15:41.139
(upbeat 80s music)

00:15:41.139 --> 00:15:43.080
Now before I get into
the meaning of the ending

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.340
and some of the deleted scenes,

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.410
there are a few more Easter
eggs I want to talk about,

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:48.000
so let's go back to the beginning.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.590
- [Zac, recording] Anytime
you watch a Halloween movie...

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:51.130
- That's not what I meant.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:53.280
(cosmic aura)

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:54.720
That is also not what I meant.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:55.553
I'm taking it back

00:15:55.553 --> 00:15:57.720
to the apparently controversial
firefighter scene.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:59.550
The name on one of the
firefighter's helmets reads Gamby.

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:02.520
Gamby was a character played
by co-writer Danny McBride

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.800
when he was on the TV
series Vice Principals.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:06.570
We can see that the fire
trucks have been painted

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.331
to say City of Haddonfield,
but the helmet says WFD,

00:16:09.331 --> 00:16:12.300
or Wilmington Fire Department,
the unit from Wilmington,

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:14.040
North Carolina where the movie was filmed.

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:16.410
CinemaSins, you can stand back up now.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.690
That means that the gear they
use is real firefighting gear,

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:21.570
so these E31 helmets are
probably just a coincidence,

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:22.740
not a reference to Halloween

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:24.630
being on October 31st or something.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:26.970
Actually, later at the bar, if
you look at this man's phone,

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:28.890
you'll see the time is now 12:07,

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:31.350
meaning we have officially
crossed into November first,

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:33.510
so the final 74 minutes
of "Halloween Kills"

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.310
don't actually take place on Halloween,

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:37.620
which is another similarity
it shares with "Halloween II,"

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:39.630
where we see the November
sunrise at the end.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:42.690
Then we see another news
report on WCZD, nice.

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:44.880
They show photos of some
of the victims from 1978,

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:46.770
including Lynda and her boyfriend, Bob.

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.050
However, for Bob, they
apparently just Googled

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:52.110
Bob 1970s high school and
found this old yearbook photo

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.790
of the actor, Bob Odenkirk.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.710
He is not the one who
played Bob in "Halloween."

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:57.000
That was John Michael Graham.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.220
But it kind of looks like
him, so they went with it.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.290
I don't know why David
Gordon Green thought Googling

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.200
Bob 1970s high school
would work, but it did.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.270
Target Halloween decorations, nice.

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:07.530
Zombie American Gothic.

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:09.390
I've done that meme before, nice!

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:10.920
Let's go back to the
kids that pull the prank

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.270
on Big John and Little John.

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:14.040
The girl claims there
was a rusty razor blade

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.270
in her sister's Halloween candy,

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:16.530
which she got at their house.

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.330
If you've seen my
"Halloween" 2018 episode,

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:19.410
you'll recognize that their masks

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.640
are the Silver Shamrock masks

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.320
from "Halloween III: Season of the Witch."

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:23.670
However, these are not the same kids

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:25.260
that we saw in "Halloween" 2018.

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:26.820
If you look at the Skeleton kid's ribcage,

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.110
it's clearly a different costume.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:30.450
But anyway, the girl claims
there was a rusty razor blade

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:31.710
in her sister's Halloween candy,

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:34.080
which she got at Big John
and Little John's house.

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:35.640
Little John is dressed up as a pirate.

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:37.440
In "Halloween II," a
kid dressed as a pirate

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:39.780
goes to the hospital after
biting into a razor blade.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.100
During the panic at the hospital,

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:43.465
one cop informs the chief that
they have called for backup.

00:17:43.465 --> 00:17:45.801
- We've requested backup
officers and medical staff

00:17:45.801 --> 00:17:48.540
from Russellville and
Eaton County for support,

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:49.551
but no confirmation.

00:17:49.551 --> 00:17:50.580
- I feel like I've probably said this

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:51.450
a million times by now,

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:53.690
but Russellville is a reference
to a line from "Halloween I"

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.110
where the gravekeeper
tells a story that happened

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:56.580
in the nearby town of Russellville.

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:57.930
Russellville was a city in Kentucky

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.670
near where John Carpenter went to college.

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.470
We get another scene with the
two Johns later that morning,

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.050
where they hear more
noises outside the house.

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:06.210
- Next time, I'm coming with a pitchfork.

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:07.380
- This is foreshadowing.

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:09.180
I already mentioned it, but
there's a moment towards the end

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:10.230
where Karen saves her daughter

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.939
by absolutely impaling
Michael with the pitchfork.

00:18:12.939 --> 00:18:15.522
(Karen grunts)

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:17.243
LOL.

00:18:17.243 --> 00:18:18.510
The sound effect used even shows us

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:19.770
that it's a real metal pitchfork,

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:21.957
not just a plastic Halloween decoration.

00:18:21.957 --> 00:18:23.070
(pitchfork clangs)

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:24.720
There's a scene in the
dining room where Little John

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:26.130
gets spooked by his own reflection,

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:27.060
but in front of the mirror,

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:28.530
there's this guillotine decoration.

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:30.060
This is one of those
things where it could be

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.460
just a Halloween decoration,
or it could be a little nod

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.600
to the famous beheading scene

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:35.550
from "Halloween H20: 20 Years Later."

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:36.810
I do have Jimmy here still.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:39.300
I am requiring him to stay
until the end of the video,

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.620
even though he already said his part.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:42.348
Jimmy, what are your thoughts on this?

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:44.310
- Wait, what?

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.143
- There's also a glimpse

00:18:45.143 --> 00:18:46.710
into the remodeled upstairs bedroom.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:48.960
This is Judith's old room, and
there's a very similar desk

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.090
with a mirror and lamp in
the same corner where Judith

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:53.910
was brushing her hair on
that fatal evening in 1963.

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:56.970
When Little John encounters
The Shape, he says this.

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:59.190
- [Little John] Michael, you've come home.

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:00.840
- Which seems to be an
homage to Loomis' line

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.941
in the first film.

00:19:01.941 --> 00:19:03.390
- He came home!

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:04.260
- Of course, that wouldn't be

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.210
the only classic line that came back.

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:07.590
- You know, it's Halloween.

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:10.367
Everyone's entitled to one good scare.

00:19:10.367 --> 00:19:12.110
I also noticed that the street
address of the Myers house

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:13.710
is 709 in this movie.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.330
This confused me, because everyone knows

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.880
that the Myers lived at
45 Lampkin Lane, right?

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:20.512
As it turns out, I'm here
to tell you they're wrong.

00:19:20.512 --> 00:19:23.095
(tense music)

00:19:25.478 --> 00:19:29.436
(foreboding music)

00:19:29.436 --> 00:19:32.400
I guess this is kind of one of
those Mandela effect moments.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.250
After seeing the Myers address
was 709 in "Halloween Kills,"

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:36.990
just to be sure, I went back and checked.

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:39.179
And to my surprise, 45
Lampkin Lane was actually

00:19:39.179 --> 00:19:41.760
an invention of the
sequel, "Halloween II."

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:43.740
- [Cop] The old Myers
house, 45 Lampkin Lane.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.540
- [Zac] If you look back at
the original "Halloween,"

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.010
it's actually 709.

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:47.910
Kinda hard to make it out,

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:50.070
but you can clearly see
701 on the neighbor's house

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:51.270
and you can even kind of make out

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:53.640
the painted over 709 in 1963.

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:55.440
So actually, "Halloween
Kills" got it right

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.850
and "Halloween II" got it wrong.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.380
Now let's talk about the ending.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.970
Allyson and Cameron go
into the Myers house

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:00.990
after Cameron's dad,

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:03.240
and Allyson discovers
the death of Little John,

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.640
and proceeds to take the knife out of him?

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:06.780
She doesn't need a knife.

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:07.800
She already has a gun.

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:09.900
You don't bring a knife to a gunfight.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.130
You bring a clothing iron.

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:13.050
Lucky for Allyson, she's
saved by her mother,

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:15.150
after which she comments
on the everlasting presence

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:17.520
that The Boogeyman has
branded on their town.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.080
- He'll always be here, won't he?

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.730
- Even when we can't see him.

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:22.729
- This line serves as a
parallel to the words of comfort

00:20:22.729 --> 00:20:25.320
her mom offers her at the
beginning of the movie.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.163
- Dad's gone.

00:20:27.062 --> 00:20:31.873
- He'll always be with us,
even if we can't see him.

00:20:31.873 --> 00:20:33.720
- Both of these moments
comment on the tendency

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:36.090
of strong emotions to
have a long lasting power,

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:37.950
one with love and the other with fear.

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:39.240
And both of them come with Allyson

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.490
wrapped in her mother's
arms, sitting on the stairs.

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:42.990
Afterwards, we see Karen look up

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:45.210
into the right bedroom
window, Judith's old room,

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.770
and she sees the six year old version

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:48.570
of Michael Myers staring out blankly.

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:49.740
This puts her in the same camp

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:51.265
as her counterpart from
the original timeline,

00:20:51.265 --> 00:20:52.560
who saw a vision of the young,

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:55.170
costumed Michael in a
reflection at the drugstore.

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:57.090
In an early draft of "Halloween" 2018,

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:58.530
Karen was going to be named Jamie,

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:00.480
just like Laurie's daughter
in the original timeline,

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:01.860
who we meet in "Halloween 4."

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:03.660
However, they decided not to do that,

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:05.070
fearing that it would be too confusing.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:06.780
But the two versions of Laurie's daughter

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.929
do share the experience
of seeing a strange image

00:21:08.929 --> 00:21:10.710
of Michael Myers's past.

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:11.700
In January of 2022,

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.704
"Halloween Kills" was
released on physical media,

00:21:13.704 --> 00:21:15.180
along with an extended cut

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:17.790
that includes a few lengthened
scenes and additional scenes.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:20.220
The 1978 flashback with
Lonnie Elam now includes

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:21.720
an extra bit of Lonnie walking home

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:23.970
and seeing Michael Myers
peering out from behind a shrub.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.070
This is a reference to the
iconic scene in the original,

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:27.390
where Laurie briefly spots Michael

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:28.590
on the way home from school.

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:30.562
The ending of the extended
cut also brings back elements

00:21:30.562 --> 00:21:32.310
of the John Carpenter original.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.840
After Karen is taken out by Michael,

00:21:33.840 --> 00:21:35.430
she receives a call on her cell phone.

00:21:35.430 --> 00:21:36.990
It's Laurie calling from the hospital,

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:38.344
and she simply hears
the sound of breathing

00:21:38.344 --> 00:21:41.301
against a plastic mask
and knows it's Michael.

00:21:41.301 --> 00:21:45.667
(breathing)

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:49.140
She knows this because
of the call she received

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.240
on Halloween night 40
years ago to this day

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:52.897
after her friend Lynda
was strangled by Michael

00:21:52.897 --> 00:21:55.653
and she heard the same sound
over the telephone line.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:59.893
(breathing)

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:02.700
We are now as close as we will ever be

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:05.280
to the final installment,
"Halloween Ends."

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:07.560
To make sure you're caught
up on all things Halloween

00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:08.760
before going into that movie,

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.620
make sure you watch
Jimmy's video on the right

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:11.580
and drop him a sub.

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:13.440
I'm sure you will after
watching that video.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:15.390
As always, I'll be going
in depth with everything

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:17.190
you might have missed in Halloween Ends.

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:19.410
Make sure you don't miss it
by subscribing to CZsWorld

00:22:19.410 --> 00:22:20.790
for new horrors every week,

00:22:20.790 --> 00:22:22.740
ring the deathbell for all notifications,

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:24.660
and I will see you in the next one.

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:26.523
Assuming we both survive.

